# Data and generated outputs (reproducible via scripts/run_all.py)
#
# Raw vendor data stays out: it is large, often licensed, and redistributing
# it would breach most providers' terms. The DERIVED research record does not
# — see below.
data/*
!data/real_data_manifest.md
!data/import/
data/import/*
!data/import/README.md

# Results: the experiment REGISTRY and the derived summary tables are the
# research record — version-controlled, because they are what makes a study
# auditable years later. Equity curves are large (~340 MB) and fully
# regenerable from the registry plus the frozen code, so they stay out.
results/*

# --- synthetic (demonstration) ---
!results/synthetic/
results/synthetic/*
!results/synthetic/experiments.jsonl
!results/synthetic/strategy_ranking.csv
!results/synthetic/company_analysis.csv
!results/synthetic/capacity.csv
!results/synthetic/robustness/
results/synthetic/robustness/*
!results/synthetic/robustness/*.csv
!results/synthetic/robustness/*.json

# --- real (the study that actually matters) ---
# These are governance artifacts, not build output. data_quality.json records
# what the gate saw and decided; holdout_lock.json is the hash-chained record
# proving the holdout was opened exactly once; run_fingerprint.json binds the
# results to a machine, a git commit and a data-store hash. A real study whose
# record is not committed is not reproducible and not auditable — which is the
# entire point of the freeze. None of these files contains vendor price data.
!results/real/
results/real/*
!results/real/experiments.jsonl
!results/real/strategy_ranking.csv
!results/real/company_analysis.csv
!results/real/capacity.csv
!results/real/data_quality.json
!results/real/import_report.json
!results/real/run_fingerprint.json
!results/real/holdout_lock.json
!results/real/robustness/
results/real/robustness/*
!results/real/robustness/*.csv
!results/real/robustness/*.json

reports/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
.env
